---
module: spec_tree
func_id: walk-func-ids
---

***conformance tests***

# func-ids-in-file-order
A :PlainSourceTree: with the functionalities f1, f2, f3, f4 yields the func-ids f1, f2, f3, f4.

# first-func-id
The first func-id of a tree with the functionalities f1, f2 is f1; a tree without `functional specs` has none.

# next-and-previous
In a tree with the single functionality simple-functionality, the next and the previous func-id of simple-functionality are both none.

# func-ids-before
The func-ids before f3 in a tree with f1, f2, f3, f4 are [f1, f2].

# has-acceptance-tests
A tree whose second functionality has one acceptance scenario has acceptance tests.
- A tree whose functionalities have no acceptance scenario has none.
- An empty tree has none.

***acceptance tests***

# unknown-func-id
Asking for the next or the previous func-id of `missing` in a tree with the functionality simple-functionality raises `Functionality missing does not exist.`.
